---
title: Mute swan
---
# Mute swan

The mute swan is a large white swan of Europe and western Asia, with an orange
bill and a black basal knob larger in the male. It feeds on submerged vegetation
reached by upending, and its long neck lets it work water a metre deep that no
duck can reach. Pairs are long-lived and strongly territorial, driving other
waterfowl from a stretch of river through the breeding season. Despite the name
it is far from silent, hissing and snorting freely, and the wings throb audibly
in flight. See [[anatidae]].
